Feature: UC-003 Cancel Order

  @UC-003.6
  Scenario Outline: Should not cancel non existent order
    When cancel order with order number <orderNumber>
    Then should fail
    And error message <message>

    Examples:
      | orderNumber              | message                                        |
      | NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-99999 | Order NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-99999 does not exist. |
      | NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-88888 | Order NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-88888 does not exist. |
      | NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-77777 | Order NON-EXISTENT-ORDER-77777 does not exist. |

  @UC-003.6
  Scenario: Cannot cancel non existent order
    When cancel order with order number "non-existent-order-12345"
    Then should fail
    And error message "Order non-existent-order-12345 does not exist."

  @UC-003.6
  Scenario: Customer should not be able to cancel another customers order
    Given an order placed by customer "B"
    And logged in as customer "A"
    When cancel order
    Then should fail
    And error message "Order ${DEFAULTS.ORDER_NUMBER} does not exist."

  @UC-003.7
  Scenario: Should not cancel already cancelled order
    Given an order with status CANCELLED
    When cancel order
    Then should fail
    And error message "Order has already been cancelled"
